{"module":"path-forward","voice":"female","duration":136.9,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"The path forward","start":0.0,"end":1.29,"words":[[0.04,0.26],[0.26,0.6],[0.6,1.16]]},{"el":"intro","text":"None of this history was inevitable, and none of it is permanent.","start":2.09,"end":5.87,"words":[[2.14,2.32],[2.32,2.45],[2.45,2.63],[2.63,3.06],[3.06,3.25],[3.25,3.92],[4.14,4.32],[4.32,4.51],[4.51,4.63],[4.63,4.76],[4.76,4.88],[4.88,5.43]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Each of these remedies has a track record, and each has a role for you.","start":6.22,"end":10.59,"words":[[6.27,6.49],[6.49,6.63],[6.63,6.85],[6.85,7.35],[7.35,7.57],[7.57,7.71],[7.71,8.0],[8.0,8.43],[8.68,8.89],[8.89,9.11],[9.11,9.33],[9.33,9.47],[9.47,9.76],[9.76,9.9],[9.9,10.11]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Laws that make harassment costly","start":10.94,"end":13.14,"words":[[10.99,11.23],[11.23,11.48],[11.48,11.8],[11.8,12.54],[12.54,13.02]]},{"el":"s0","text":"San Francisco's CAREN Act, Oregon's 2019 law and California's AB 1775 give targets a remedy.","start":13.84,"end":21.87,"words":[[13.84,14.07],[14.07,14.89],[14.89,15.27],[15.27,15.57],[15.83,16.36],[16.36,17.33],[17.33,17.48],[17.48,17.71],[17.71,18.46],[18.46,18.61],[18.61,20.03],[20.03,20.26],[20.26,20.71],[20.71,20.86],[20.86,21.38]]},{"el":"s0","text":"A federal version would extend that everywhere.","start":22.22,"end":25.39,"words":[[22.27,22.41],[22.41,22.93],[22.93,23.3],[23.3,23.52],[23.52,24.03],[24.03,24.25],[24.25,24.84]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Read and improve the draft, then ask your lawmakers to introduce it.","start":25.74,"end":30.04,"words":[[25.79,26.0],[26.0,26.21],[26.21,26.64],[26.64,26.78],[26.78,27.21],[27.45,27.67],[27.67,27.88],[27.88,28.02],[28.02,28.59],[28.59,28.73],[28.73,29.37],[29.37,29.58]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Different responders","start":30.94,"end":32.36,"words":[[31.0,31.55],[31.55,32.24]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Programs like CAHOOTS (Eugene) and STAR (Denver) send medics and counselors to calls that don't need police.","start":33.06,"end":39.79,"words":[[33.11,33.74],[33.74,34.03],[34.03,34.45],[34.45,34.87],[35.12,35.33],[35.33,35.54],[35.54,35.89],[36.14,36.42],[36.42,36.84],[36.84,37.05],[37.05,37.68],[37.68,37.83],[37.83,38.11],[38.11,38.32],[38.32,38.67],[38.67,38.88],[38.88,39.3]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Ask your city council whether yours has one.","start":40.14,"end":42.57,"words":[[40.19,40.39],[40.39,40.52],[40.52,40.77],[40.77,41.23],[41.23,41.48],[41.48,41.68],[41.68,41.87],[41.87,42.13]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Telling the truth in public","start":43.47,"end":45.35,"words":[[43.53,43.98],[43.98,44.16],[44.16,44.52],[44.52,44.7],[44.7,45.24]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Truth commissions (South Africa 1996, Greensboro 2004–2006, Canada 2008–2015) and memorials like EJI's National Memorial for Peace and Justice in Montgomery put the record where everyone can see it.","start":46.05,"end":64.86,"words":[[46.1,46.45],[46.45,47.14],[47.14,47.48],[47.48,48.0],[48.0,49.56],[49.86,50.73],[50.73,53.06],[53.36,53.88],[53.88,56.13],[56.43,56.69],[56.69,57.56],[57.56,57.9],[57.9,58.25],[58.25,58.85],[58.85,59.63],[59.63,59.8],[59.8,60.06],[60.06,60.32],[60.32,60.93],[60.93,61.1],[61.1,61.97],[61.97,62.23],[62.23,62.4],[62.4,62.83],[62.83,63.09],[63.09,63.7],[63.7,63.95],[63.95,64.13],[64.13,64.39]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Teaching these modules is part of that work.","start":65.21,"end":67.64,"words":[[65.21,65.62],[65.62,65.83],[65.83,66.3],[66.3,66.44],[66.44,66.65],[66.65,66.78],[66.78,66.99],[66.99,67.26]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Repair","start":68.54,"end":69.45,"words":[[68.59,69.3]]},{"el":"s3","text":"The Civil Liberties Act of 1988 apologized and paid $20,000 to each surviving Japanese American who had been incarcerated.","start":70.15,"end":79.27,"words":[[70.2,70.35],[70.35,70.71],[70.71,71.21],[71.21,71.43],[71.43,71.57],[71.57,72.66],[72.66,73.45],[73.45,73.67],[73.67,73.96],[73.96,75.18],[75.18,75.33],[75.33,75.54],[75.54,76.12],[76.12,76.7],[76.7,77.28],[77.28,77.42],[77.42,77.64],[77.64,77.85],[77.85,78.79]]},{"el":"s3","text":"North Carolina and Virginia have compensated sterilization survivors.","start":79.62,"end":84.31,"words":[[79.67,79.87],[79.87,80.47],[80.47,80.67],[80.67,81.2],[81.2,81.4],[81.4,82.21],[82.21,83.14],[83.14,83.74]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Evanston, Illinois, began housing reparations in 2021, California's Reparations Task Force issued its final report in 2023, and H.R.","start":84.66,"end":96.79,"words":[[84.71,85.43],[85.71,86.28],[86.56,86.96],[86.96,87.44],[87.44,88.33],[88.33,88.49],[88.49,89.77],[90.06,90.86],[90.86,91.74],[91.74,92.07],[92.07,92.31],[92.31,92.63],[92.63,92.87],[92.87,93.35],[93.35,93.76],[93.76,93.92],[93.92,95.2],[95.48,95.73],[95.73,96.21]]},{"el":"s3","text":"40 would create a federal commission.","start":97.14,"end":99.43,"words":[[97.16,97.4],[97.4,97.58],[97.58,97.99],[97.99,98.11],[98.11,98.53],[98.53,99.01]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Whether and how to do more is debated; the precedents are documented.","start":99.78,"end":103.84,"words":[[99.82,100.08],[100.08,100.27],[100.27,100.46],[100.46,100.59],[100.59,100.72],[100.72,100.85],[100.85,100.98],[100.98,101.56],[101.78,101.91],[101.91,102.56],[102.56,102.62],[102.62,103.4]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Clearing the books","start":104.74,"end":106.15,"words":[[104.74,105.43],[105.43,105.62],[105.62,106.02]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Segregation-era language still sits in some codes and deeds.","start":106.85,"end":111.14,"words":[[106.88,108.03],[108.03,108.65],[108.65,108.96],[108.96,109.27],[109.27,109.42],[109.42,109.66],[109.66,110.04],[110.04,110.27],[110.27,110.66]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Volunteers can verify old laws and deliver repeal requests, and many states now let homeowners strike covenants from their deeds.","start":111.49,"end":120.08,"words":[[111.54,112.22],[112.22,112.44],[112.44,112.97],[112.97,113.27],[113.27,113.49],[113.49,113.72],[113.72,114.17],[114.17,114.55],[114.55,115.22],[115.48,115.71],[115.71,116.01],[116.01,116.46],[116.46,116.69],[116.69,116.91],[116.91,117.59],[117.59,118.04],[118.04,118.71],[118.71,119.02],[119.02,119.24],[119.24,119.62]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Showing up locally","start":120.98,"end":122.31,"words":[[121.03,121.43],[121.43,121.59],[121.59,122.15]]},{"el":"s5","text":"District attorneys, sheriffs and city councils decide how the police are used, and they are often elected by a few thousand votes.","start":123.01,"end":131.09,"words":[[123.06,123.64],[123.64,124.14],[124.4,124.83],[124.83,125.05],[125.05,125.34],[125.34,125.92],[125.92,126.36],[126.36,126.58],[126.58,126.72],[126.72,127.08],[127.08,127.16],[127.16,127.52],[127.77,127.99],[127.99,128.21],[128.21,128.28],[128.28,128.57],[128.57,129.08],[129.08,129.3],[129.3,129.44],[129.44,129.66],[129.66,130.17],[130.17,130.61]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Register, check your registration, and vote in local elections.","start":131.44,"end":135.96,"words":[[131.49,132.08],[132.31,132.57],[132.57,132.7],[132.7,133.62],[133.85,134.05],[134.05,134.31],[134.31,134.44],[134.44,134.84],[134.84,135.43]]}]}